// A carrier PRVALUE coerces into a const char* position exactly like a named
// carrier: a functional-cast temporary `value("t")`, a by-value `var` return,
// and a varargs argument each pass the carrier's text (madarray_cstr), never
// the temporary's storage words. The call lowering admitted only LVALUE
// carriers to the c_str coercion: the three prvalue lines printed empty
// strings (c2mir "incompatible pointer types of argument and parameter" on
// the two declared-parameter calls, no diagnostic at all on the varargs one).
// .expect_quiet gates the warning.
// Oracle — the explicit-c_str C++ analogue (a class with c_str();
// f(value("temp").c_str()), f(make().c_str()),
// printf("%s\n", value("vararg").c_str())): g++ -std=c++17 and
// clang++ -std=c++17 both print named / temp / made / vararg.
void f(const char *s) { println("{}", s); }
var make() { var r = "made"; return r; }
int main() {
	var v = "named";
	f(v);
	f(value("temp"));
	f(make());
	printf("%s\n", value("vararg"));
	return 0;
}
